.TH HYPRCURSOR-UTIL 1 "hyprcursor-util" "hyprcursor-util" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
hyprcursor-util \- compile, pack, and extract hyprcursor and xcursor themes

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprcursor-util
.RI [ options ] " command " [ path ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprcursor-util
is a utility for compiling, packing, unpacking, and converting cursor themes
between hyprcursor, xcursor, and a working-state representation.

The working state is an easy-to-navigate format where each cursor is stored as
a PNG or SVG and metadata is stored in files.

.SH RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
.B hyprcursor-util
uses
.B xcur2png
at runtime.

.SH THEME STATES
Themes may exist in the following states:

.TP
.B compiled hyprcursor
Usable by applications and compositors supporting hyprcursor.

.TP
.B compiled xcursor
Usable by xcursor-based software.

.TP
.B working state
Editable form where each cursor is a PNG or SVG and metadata is stored in files.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "--create " path
.TQ
.BI "-c " path
Create a compiled hyprcursor theme from a working-state directory.

.TP
.BI "--extract " path
.TQ
.BI "-x " path
Extract an xcursor theme into a working-state directory.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--output " directory
.TQ
.BI "-o " directory
Specify the output directory.

For safety reasons, do not use this option with versions below 0.1.1, as those
versions remove the specified directory without confirmation.

Since version 0.1.2, the specified output directory is treated as the parent
directory, and the result is written to a subdirectory named:

.PP
.RS
.I $ACTION_$NAME
.RE

.TP
.BI "--resize " mode
For
.B --extract
only, specify the default resize algorithm for shapes.

The default is
.BR none .

.SH EXAMPLES
Create a compiled hyprcursor theme from a working-state directory:
.PP
.nf
hyprcursor-util --create ./theme-workdir
.fi

.PP
Create a compiled hyprcursor theme and place the result under a chosen parent
directory:
.PP
.nf
hyprcursor-util --create ./theme-workdir --output ./out
.fi

.PP
Extract an xcursor theme into a working-state directory:
.PP
.nf
hyprcursor-util --extract ./xcursor-theme
.fi

.PP
Extract using a resize mode:
.PP
.nf
hyprcursor-util --extract ./xcursor-theme --resize none
.fi

.SH NOTES
The
.B --output
behavior changed in version 0.1.2. In that and later versions, the named
directory is treated as a parent directory rather than the final destination.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xcur2png (1)

